To improve the component integration and reduce overhead, you can leverage design patterns that promote loose coupling and high cohesion. One effective pattern for managing component integration is the **Facade Pattern**, which provides a simplified interface to a complex subsystem. Another useful pattern is the **Observer Pattern**, which can help manage dependencies between components.

### Facade Pattern

The Facade Pattern provides a unified interface to a set of interfaces in a subsystem. This can simplify the client interaction with the subsystem and reduce the complexity of the integration.

### Observer Pattern

The Observer Pattern defines a one-to-many dependency between objects so that when one object changes state, all its dependents are notified and updated automatically. This can help manage dependencies between components and reduce overhead.

### Implementation

Let's implement both patterns to improve the component integration:

#### Facade Pattern

We'll create a facade class that encapsulates the complexity of integrating multiple components.

#### Observer Pattern

We'll use the Observer Pattern to manage dependencies between components.

