Integrating a circular buffer with ROS 2 for data transfer involves several steps. You'll need to set up a ROS 2 node to receive Lidar data, then use that data to populate the circular buffer. Here's a step-by-step guide to achieve this integration:

### Step 1: Set Up ROS 2 Node

First, create a ROS 2 node that subscribes to the Lidar data topic. This node will receive the Lidar data and pass it to the circular buffer.

#### 1.1 Create a ROS 2 Node

Create a new ROS 2 package and a node to handle the Lidar data subscription.

