APlayerCharacter::APlayerCharacter()
{
    // Initialization code
}

void APlayerCharacter::BeginPlay()
{
    Super::BeginPlay();

    m_playerHealth = 100.0f; // Initialize player health
    m_enemyPosition = FVector(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f); // Initialize enemy position
}

void APlayerCharacter::UpdatePlayerHealth(float DeltaHealth)
{
    m_playerHealth += DeltaHealth;
    if (m_playerHealth < 0.0f)
    {
        m_playerHealth = 0.0f;
    }
}

void APlayerCharacter::MoveEnemy(FVector NewPosition)
{
    m_enemyPosition = NewPosition;
}
```

### Benefits of Consistent Naming Conventions

1. **Readability**:
   - Consistent naming conventions make the code easier to read and understand.

2. **Maintainability**:
   - It is easier to maintain and modify code when naming conventions are consistent.

3. **Collaboration**:
   - Team members can work more effectively together when everyone follows the same conventions.

4. **Tool Support**:
   - Many IDEs and code analysis tools can better support and highlight code when consistent conventions are followed.

### Transitioning to a Single Convention

If you are currently using a mix of naming conventions, you can transition to a single convention by:

1. **Updating Existing Code**:
   - Gradually update existing code to follow the chosen convention. This can be done incrementally as you work on different parts of the project.

2. **Code Reviews**:
   - Enforce the new convention during code reviews to ensure consistency moving forward.

3. **Automated Tools**:
   - Use automated tools and scripts to help identify and update inconsistent naming conventions.

